{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0385d37866a63894f262dca3a002077ddb37e023ae5803fe01bd8c9bc847f5ab","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_28230a1f03803257fb92170799820f76fb2b749283a8cd1225714ac0d9569177","slc_d5714b4a85d764d3d99e4e3ba0605cc8fb9cbef5bde5be18082388e5afa57ae2"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Updates run via /update in the TUI or `jcode update`; dev builds compare the running binary's Git commit against the release tag and stop rather than risk a downgrade when ancestry cannot be verified.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0dc258fa4732a92229eba3bc9faa2d4ba08da316ae3d719c4f3030657196a529","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_77cddaa116ba669fbf08cea045a8225d22c829752a0fbc3d792e8e707781ada1"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"jcode currently supports only stdio (command-based) MCP servers; HTTP/SSE entries are recognized and skipped with a log line.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_17707422749be4f1f2051cd4ff5d261b46a5237d84496d4ca284af084a492e14","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_024f35bb933d3451c8e78d39525dfd493f1ba03736b6e2e003c91c3728ee0d98"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"User input is interleaved with the working agent as soon as it can be sent without breaking the KV cache; shift-enter instead queues the message until the agent finishes its turn.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_19f58047b4b99221f073f6d7dc26569123c7ba80507fb7dfb645ed33cf625183","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3adf6397bc50d90c49f35089f1736d5fb42ebedb6db760d5d48fd680ebbe4636","slc_6860ed09523dc38f0ff6c19266788184bac1c07b413551cc77de9bc31dafb244","slc_c7c201948d75f16eadcbaff36c78f6cb7e52a76ac9d7d758e4255950aa2ff61c"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"The README reports self-measured benchmarks: jcode at 14.0 ms time-to-first-frame and 48.7 ms time-to-first-input versus slower figures for Codex CLI, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor Agent, and others, across 10 interactive PTY launches on one Linux machine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1f452482d459dd2daa950150229f9c172a02906230f3beb49f31ddcad4b06ae1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_415fc313ddd94b84d3e062596e7a54d0814cc5a25f4219900b34b1a7929c33b8","slc_7f8fde1d85b4471d532986d49ae19b105d46ee5967f75208fcc11d1cec21842a","slc_c9baa248870be85ae8da4066a07c2a185a9c5b76f8efd28bc85b4e79946f8741"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"MCP servers are configured in ~/.jcode/mcp.json (global) and .jcode/mcp.json (project-local); Claude Code config files (~/.claude.json, .mcp.json, .claude/mcp.json) are read live, and a one-time import from ~/.codex/config.toml is performed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e0adbd6ce51b05c6f2d4d1f6234706c1011a17c36a8530edefbd67001bdb400","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_45621a313931a309eb6a58e5f49e2a28a133155a15d49563ec69f35984863121"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Multiple agents spawned in the same repo are managed by a server: when one agent edits a file another has read, the server notifies the reader, which can ignore it or check the diff; agents can DM, broadcast, or message repo-scoped peers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4b31bb09421f7fd4a18d467167ae822772ff4a3546a6a76301388ffa285661b1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_589c05cec6096be9672277f2d40a951af91d4525962ce22ca8819e1e1c05808b"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Smooth partial-line scrolling is not possible with jcode's custom scrollback in normal terminals due to a terminal-level limitation; the author's separate Handterm terminal with a native scroll API is a work in progress addressing this.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_882610b9676cf4753adab4f2c626c4225531e12cc5205089b5e0efb0d26b6048","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_18eacb2001e4c88a03d72d68d7c6cad6b45859b1c00d27ca8bb20300454d4d9d"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Besides passive background recall, jcode provides explicit memory tools for active search/store, plus session search performing traditional RAG over previous sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8a5ded1a1c5b93ca80c76384e555bc464ac45aeebf72322a9a6605fb24a0f77e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_80d5817d59778f5a55aba7deeb018b8cecb21cd8f51fd55c5aa35d9f28190e5b"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"jcode offers built-in login flows via `jcode login --provider <id>` for providers including claude, openai, gemini, copilot, azure, fireworks, novita, minimax, lmstudio, ollama, and custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ade5080eaf55fd5d31ad6fa69138bf5b3a981a0fab3661047f7d99e6b6efcd6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d3a483b6d33160223271fe41a6c8599ce783d5b9ab01da15aba94159ebf0692"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Each conversation turn is embedded as a semantic vector and queried against a memory graph via cosine similarity; hits are injected into the conversation, optionally after verification by a memory sideagent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8c7d255f2686db133ffc6430b5e57137d9ff644101c1a5efb4e457729e319c5c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d3a483b6d33160223271fe41a6c8599ce783d5b9ab01da15aba94159ebf0692"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Memories are extracted by a memory sideagent at triggers such as semantic drift, a K-turn interval, or session end, and added to the memory graph.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_946e9862b151210f9e8e21927e398d7321c285fe58037da8ce21403c3ad7eb2e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fcfa204de0e16357d13d21852631f345b47ef13eb1577c2a84de8ea4b3e9b01f"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Skills are not all loaded at startup; embedding hits on the conversation inject relevant skills automatically, and skills can also be activated manually via a skill tool or slash commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_97ee62fef9916269e668e2a36f42572e7a030d34e3e231b5138b45c402cc8c28","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_282d32bd1e72fdc4e30edb5768b5a66854e46e11827d29780ff984d9c894e0ec","slc_c675d3bc91839820d764082ff0b267d2799c83db6616946ceac08a6275c4751e"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"A memory-scaling comparison reports ~9.9-10.4 MB extra PSS per added jcode session versus larger figures for competing tools, with tested versions listed (e.g. jcode v0.9.1888-dev, codex-cli 0.120.0, Claude Code 2.1.86).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a133509c1534db3799addcdf629d5139f7dd41f5ada37c9dd1cb8038e7e4c7f6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8225cbf7e16059afb34f5d0effc747f1563bde4a76bf73345436776040aa666f"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Agents have a swarm tool to autonomously spawn teammates for parallel work, turning the main agent into a coordinator; groups, messaging channels, and completion statuses are managed automatically, headed or headless.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a37ac9b968663d997b15d6d4b41befb623754fd2f6ad7a1d146a64c157e241d8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5a100f68548427932f89f1f65b3f1011899042c162eef9815aa1cf5fd3d1ce4b"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"An 'agent grep' tool augments grep output with file structure information (function lists, offsets) and adaptively truncates results based on what the agent has already seen to save context.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e3923c2064cf33c4bb6802dd198b485082c3ef9c22f63b33bb819cb503afe6d1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_077743e5d29dd7f30c5088405c10fdc98f4c740b763577c916f8df950742aa21","slc_157c90f6bedb99acbe4c3fa7227438f23fa883698c88644da1df43aae6594f25","slc_6d16e7c04b0cacf55c8cafcad8595eb6318ab9c76fb74e12dff52cc457fcd662","slc_eb261a48d1f6d0ac60e7ee0466bdebe6b5007d5301b494b820a5792e89e4d468"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"Headless OAuth is supported via --no-browser (printing auth URL/QR for manual paste), and a two-step --print-auth-url / --callback-url or --auth-code pattern exists for openai, gemini, claude, and antigravity.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f5c2440557548e283a75276e3dceb87733471b3fa63efe430c3e7da4856609a7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_469ce9359073a46e2aba03b71fe962ed0f44b6cf79d8ffbd31a41b9960b07fe8"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"The side panel can display files updated in real time, receive agent-written content, act as a diff viewer, and render mermaid diagrams inline in both panel and chat.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f675a67985250349fafd70ccc92c0370485350ded68446fc7c749e17a1dcc20b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"1jehuang/jcode@37159430c3d0 snapshot b7be00436905e014","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e589ce2ea817ee4babe3e896d25267acff2330efc3414ba8935a1493bb4aa23"],"source_ids":["src_57e5fe2c807c5815812977626e431470"],"text":"An ambient mode periodically consolidates memories, reorganizing them and checking for staleness and conflicts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:58:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_981d8a7b4711404a99cb46f533b71b4f"}
